                                "example_id": "949de8ce-37b7-446e-811e-9d0764912d2a",
                                "sense_id": "884b8d21-319b-3c89-a244-805d29f810df",
                                "text": "c. 1565-1570, George Turberville, A Lover's Vow\nWhen hawks shall dread the silly fowl, / And men esteem the nightish owl"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b103b59-f0a3-4ac2-89d3-3248830a78d5",
                                "sense_id": "884b8d21-319b-3c89-a244-805d29f810df",
                                "text": "Star light's nights twinkling. Moonlight is nightish, Sun makes day: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6966958-bed4-495a-b783-bdaa3b67219f",
                                "sense_id": "884b8d21-319b-3c89-a244-805d29f810df",
                                "text": "Nightish folk working their sleepingcity functions in the bright squares of office windows. People untouched by day, smugly snug. You wonder at this darker world of theirs. You grow querulous and bewildered."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
